Janis Papanagnou <Janis_Papanagnou@hotmail.com> writes:
> I dare to take over the thread to extend your question; why would
> one do the following which is documented in the source as follows...
> 
>    "The Heart of Ahriman", LUCKSTONE
>    /* this stone does double damage if used as a projectile weapon */

This is more accidental than anything else, I think. Prior to 3.4.0 it
was defined as NO_ATTK, which happens to be #defined as having the
same value if you treat it _as_ an attack type as PHYS(0,0); and an
attk.damd of 0 for AD_PHYS means "double damage". I think the DevTeam
just overlooked the fact that it could be used in combat at all; when
Darshan and I pointed it out to them, they decided to rationalise it
as "er, yeah, that was intentional, honest" and changed it to an
actual PHYS() attack value (giving it +5 to-hit while they were at
it).

